msgid "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION\nTEST: metal-support pump cycles preceded strikes; no talk link."
msgstr "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION\nTEST: metal-support pump cycles preceded strikes; no talk link."

msgid "TEST support comparison: apply equal small impulses through metal and padded supports; keep airborne pump sound and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Strike bursts follow metal-support impulses more often than padded-support impulses. Airborne pump sound is unchanged; slow wall tracing persists on both supports. This test does not compare airflow cycles."
msgstr "TEST support comparison: apply equal small impulses through metal and padded supports; keep airborne pump sound and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Strike bursts follow metal-support impulses more often than padded-support impulses. Airborne pump sound is unchanged; slow wall tracing persists on both supports. This test does not compare airflow cycles."

msgid "TEST airflow comparison: compare continuous low airflow with repeated start/stop pulses; keep support and pump sound unchanged.\nResult: Start/stop airflow prompts repeated turn-backs toward the outlet; continuous low airflow produces fewer turn-backs. Wall tracing persists in both trials. This test does not compare support isolation."
msgstr "TEST airflow comparison: compare continuous low airflow with repeated start/stop pulses; keep support and pump sound unchanged.\nResult: Start/stop airflow prompts repeated turn-backs toward the outlet; continuous low airflow produces fewer turn-backs. Wall tracing persists in both trials. This test does not compare support isolation."

msgid "TEST sound comparison: replay pump sound through a speaker while support impulses and airflow changes are absent.\nResult: The subject briefly orients toward the speaker, but the replay does not reproduce the pump-start strike bursts. Wall tracing continues. Airborne sound alone does not explain the earlier timing link."
msgstr "TEST sound comparison: replay pump sound through a speaker while support impulses and airflow changes are absent.\nResult: The subject briefly orients toward the speaker, but the replay does not reproduce the pump-start strike bursts. Wall tracing continues. Airborne sound alone does not explain the earlier timing link."

msgid "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION CASE 02\nTEST: wall-contact loss precedes searching; no damage recorded."
msgstr "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION CASE 02\nTEST: wall-contact loss precedes searching; no damage recorded."

msgid "TEST cue comparison: deliver short air pulses from a fixed nozzle, then replay fan sound alone. Keep wall surface and lighting unchanged.\nResult: Air pulses repeatedly prompt a pivot toward the nozzle and then wall tracing resumes. Fan sound alone produces no consistent pivot. This test does not establish whether wall texture affects searching."
msgstr "TEST cue comparison: deliver short air pulses from a fixed nozzle, then replay fan sound alone. Keep wall surface and lighting unchanged.\nResult: Air pulses repeatedly prompt a pivot toward the nozzle and then wall tracing resumes. Fan sound alone produces no consistent pivot. This test does not establish whether wall texture affects searching."

msgid "TEST surface comparison: present adjacent shallow-ribbed and smooth wall panels under the same airflow and lighting; record paw tracks and contact pressure.\nResult: Across repeated passes, paw tracks follow shallow ribs and return to the same wall path. On the smooth panel, sideways searches repeatedly reach the service grille. Contact pressure does not increase on either panel. This test does not compare continuous and start/stop airflow."
msgstr "TEST surface comparison: present adjacent shallow-ribbed and smooth wall panels under the same airflow and lighting; record paw tracks and contact pressure.\nResult: Across repeated passes, paw tracks follow shallow ribs and return to the same wall path. On the smooth panel, sideways searches repeatedly reach the service grille. Contact pressure does not increase on either panel. This test does not compare continuous and start/stop airflow."

msgid "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION CASE 03\nTEST: follows contrasting floor strips; short pauses occur at gaps."
msgstr "Classification: TEST CLASSIFICATION CASE 03\nTEST: follows contrasting floor strips; short pauses occur at gaps."

msgid "TEST: compare contrasting and low-contrast strips on the same flat floor with lighting and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Travel tracks the contrasting strip for more of each pass. On the low-contrast strip, short pauses and turns recur. This observation does not establish long-term containment."
msgstr "TEST: compare contrasting and low-contrast strips on the same flat floor with lighting and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Travel tracks the contrasting strip for more of each pass. On the low-contrast strip, short pauses and turns recur. This observation does not establish long-term containment."

msgid "TEST: compare continuous and interrupted contrasting strips while keeping floor texture, lighting and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Continuous strips support longer uninterrupted passes. Gaps prompt pauses and short turns before the subject finds the next visible strip. Responses to changes in lighting remain untested."
msgstr "TEST: compare continuous and interrupted contrasting strips while keeping floor texture, lighting and airflow unchanged.\nResult: Continuous strips support longer uninterrupted passes. Gaps prompt pauses and short turns before the subject finds the next visible strip. Responses to changes in lighting remain untested."

